:" The feed and a consumer in one process: 200 trades at 400 a second with seed 7.
   The output is the same on every run. The program ends after the summary: the
   consumer closes its connection, and the last client leaving stops the server.

   kgpy demo.kg [-- port] "

where:::[(#.os.argv);.os.argv@0;"18888"]
.os.argv::[;where;"400";"200";"7"]
.l("feed.kg")
.os.argv::[;where;"AAPL";"NVDA";"TSLA"]
.l("consumer.kg")

closed::.srv.c
.srv.c::{closed(x);:[0=#subs;.srv(0);0]}
